# HCTL_HC_PBB40C_20DP_0_4V_02 - component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint, LCSC
# pinned in properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields).
#
# NEW PART (2026-07-26, Middleweight encoder-daughterboard re-architecture). HCTL
# HC-PBB40C series 0.4mm-pitch board-to-board PLUG (DP = male half), 20 contacts dual-row
# + 4 corner fitting nails (pads 21-24, grounded per the N17 precedent). This is the MAIN
# BOARD half of the encoder-daughterboard interconnect - the exact part the proven MnB
# Ultralight N17 used for the same job (N17 main board U9, LCSC id read from the N17
# .kicad_pcb footprint field; the connectors were physically ordered for the N17 - LCSC
# order artifact SO12510046049 sits in the N17 encoder project dir).
#
# Mates with HC-PBB40C-20DS-0.4V-2.5-02 (parts/HCTL_HC_PBB40C_20DS_0_4V_2_5_02.zen) for a
# 2.5mm MATED STACK HEIGHT (the socket P/N's -2.5 suffix; easyeda2kicad model heights:
# plug 1.14mm + socket 1.94mm, interpenetrating to 2.5). Pad field 5.27 x 2.02mm
# (incl. nails), body ~5.2 x 3.2mm.
#
# MATED PIN PAIRING (derived from the N17's own net assignments across both boards,
# both halves placed rot180 on their boards' BACK sides, daughterboard flipped onto the
# main board): plug even pin n <-> socket even pin (22-n); plug odd pin n <-> socket odd
# pin (20-n). Replicate the N17's relative placement (same rotation for both halves) and
# geometry-verify at layout time - do not re-derive by hand.
#
